    notes:
      'Built from TB2 Chapters 2, 3 and 11, combining the analytical thread that runs through the first two chapters with the static force treatment of Chapter 11. The module is the hinge of the course: the first half completes the kinematics by replacing drawing with algebra, and the second half asks the first question about force. The two halves belong together because the analytical position and velocity solution is exactly what a force analysis needs as its input, and because both are what a computer actually does when a mechanism is simulated. Virtual work is placed last because it answers the question a designer usually asks, namely what input torque is required, without computing a single pin reaction. All page numbers are 5th-edition pages; see the edition notice in the file header.',
